  "question": {
    "text": "Let a plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> pass through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and contain the line, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math> If distance of the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> from the origin is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The required plane passes through the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Assume, the equation of the plane is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>The line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;lies on the required plane.</p><p>So, we can say that&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Use cross-multiplication to solve the equations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>b</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp; (Assume)</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math></p><p>Put the values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;in the required equation of plane we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>So, the distance of the plane from the origin is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mn>3</mn></mfenced><msqrt><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
}